---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { documentedComponents } from "../../data/components";
import { Link } from "../../../registry/ui/link";

const principles = [
  [
    "You own the code.",
    "Components are copied into your project, not installed as a runtime dependency. Edit them freely.",
  ],
  [
    "Accessible by default.",
    "Every component targets WCAG 2.2 AA and follows its WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices pattern.",
  ],
  [
    "Platform first.",
    "Native elements, the popover attribute and semantic HTML come before any JavaScript workaround.",
  ],
  [
    "Built from scratch.",
    "No headless UI library underneath: focus, keyboard and ARIA behavior are written and tested here.",
  ],
  [
    "Themeable.",
    "Components use the standard shadcn tokens only, so a new palette needs no component changes.",
  ],
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Introduction | Buril UI"
  description="What Buril UI is, the principles behind it and where to start."
>
  <h1 class="font-display text-3xl">Introduction</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-muted-foreground">
    Buril UI is a set of accessible React components that you copy into your project, then read,
    change and keep.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">What it is</h2>
  <p class="mt-4">
    Buril is a shadcn-compatible registry, not a package. The shadcn CLI copies a component's source
    into your project, next to your own code, and installs the few npm packages it needs. From then
    on the file is yours: there is no version to upgrade and no styling API to work around.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4">
    The components are written with React and Tailwind CSS and read the same design tokens as
    shadcn/ui, so they sit next to shadcn components in the same project.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Principles</h2>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
    {principles.map(([title, body]) => (
      <li>
        <strong>{title}</strong> {body}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Status</h2>
  <p class="mt-4">
    Buril is in early development. {documentedComponents.length} components are documented, each
    with tests and a page. The registry is not hosted yet, so install commands use the placeholder
    domain
    <code>example.com</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Next steps</h2>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
    <li>
      <Link href="/docs/installation">Installation</Link>: add your first component.
    </li>
    <li>
      <Link href="/docs/theming">Theming</Link>: the tokens, dark mode and the optional palette.
    </li>
    <li>
      <Link href="/docs/components">Components</Link>: every component, with live demos.
    </li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
